# ===================================================================
# DATA: deny by default.
#
# This harness scores model outputs against human labels for True's
# call-centre apps. The ground-truth workbooks carry customer phone
# numbers and verbatim call-content snippets. Nothing derived from
# them may ever be committed.
#
# These rules ignore DIRECTORIES, not extensions, on purpose: a pandas
# pipeline emits .parquet, .jsonl, .feather and .ipynb as readily as
# .csv, and a notebook's stored cell outputs embed real rows. An
# extension allowlist leaks the first time someone uses a new format.
#
# There are deliberately NO negation exceptions. An exception is a
# hole, and there is nothing in these directories worth tracking.
#
# The real control is the runtime refusal in src/evalharness/paths.py:
# EVAL_HARNESS_DATA_DIR has no default and must resolve OUTSIDE any
# git worktree. This file is the second line of defence.
# ===================================================================
data/
out/
build/

# Belt and braces: raw workbooks and extracts anywhere in the tree, not just
# inside data/ and out/. Ground-truth workbooks arrive as .xlsx; .xlsm is
# blocked too in case a macro-enabled copy shows up. Blanket rather than
# name-matched, because a real workbook saved under any filename outside
# data/ or out/ must still be caught. tests/fixtures/*.csv is synthetic
# (08100000xx) and IS tracked, so csv is not blanket-ignored.
*.xlsx
*.xlsm
**/Post Evaluate*
**/*_PRIVATE.*
**/*NAMED-PRIVATE*

# ===================================================================
# Secrets
# EVAL_HARNESS_KEY_HMAC salts the item key. True's team holds it and
# resolves hashes back to calls inside their systems. It never lives here.
# ===================================================================
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
/env
*.pem
*.key
credentials.json
secrets.json
**/secrets/

# One narrow exception, and only one. A server's TLS CERTIFICATE is public by
# construction -- it is handed to every client that connects, so committing it discloses
# nothing that a `curl` would not. Token Factory's is self-signed, so pinning it is what
# lets the probes VERIFY the connection instead of falling back to `verify=False`, which
# would give up the guarantee that the host is the intended one on a connection carrying
# a bearer token. Committing it makes verification possible; the `*.pem` rule above is
# about PRIVATE KEYS, which this is not and which stay ignored.
#
# Un-ignore this file BY NAME rather than relaxing `*.pem`: the next `.pem` to appear
# should still have to argue for itself.
!configs/token-factory.crt.pem

# ===================================================================
# Python
# ===================================================================
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
dist/
*.egg
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.tox/
.nox/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
coverage.xml
pip-log.txt

# Generated Token Factory error logs. `scripts/token_factory_error_log.sh` writes a new
# timestamped file on every run, and they accumulate fast while an outage is being chased.
# A specific outage worth keeping is committed under a stable name instead -- see
# docs/token-factory-outage-2026-08-16.txt, which cannot be regenerated once the backend
# recovers.
docs/token-factory-error-log-*.txt

# Virtual environments
.venv/
.venv-asr/
venv/
env/
ENV/
.python-version

# ===================================================================
# Jupyter: outputs embed DataFrame reprs of real rows
# ===================================================================
.ipynb_checkpoints/
*.ipynb

# ===================================================================
# IDE, editors and AI-tool local config
# ===================================================================
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
*.sublime-project
*.sublime-workspace

# Claude Code's project directory: local settings plus, in practice, a mix
# of marketplace-installed skills and machine-specific state, not authored
# project content. Ignored wholesale, same treatment as .idea/ and .vscode/
# above rather than a special case.
.claude/

# ===================================================================
# OS
# ===================================================================
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini

# Windows: the alternate-data-stream marker left on any file downloaded
# through a browser. Harmless, but it has no business in a commit.
*:Zone.Identifier

# ===================================================================
# Logs, temp, scratch
# ===================================================================
*.log
logs/
tmp/
temp/
*.tmp
*.bak
Untitled.*
~$*

# ===================================================================
# True's production source: TRACKED, by deliberate reversal.
#
# Until 2026-08-05 this repository blocked the directory outright
# ("must NEVER live in this repository"), after a workflow agent copied
# 635 files / 15MB of it here by accident on 2026-08-04 -- a copy that
# didn't even work, since production_ref.py resolved TRUE_SOURCE_ROOT to
# a directory outside the repo and the test skipped regardless.
#
# Decision, 2026-08-05, by the owner: keep it, on purpose this time. It is
# True's Gemini-calling production source across four apps (Retention,
# MNP, RTR fraud, sentiment-voice-analysis) and is the thing every
# `rule_*` citation in tests/fixtures/testsets/ and every file:line
# reference across src/evalgen/ resolves against -- committing it turns
# those citations from "trust me" into something a reviewer can open.
# Scanned before commit: no .env/.pem/.key/credentials files and no
# live-API-key-shaped strings found in the tree.
#
# Renamed source-code-review/ -> production-reference/ the same day: the
# old name read as a temporary review copy, which this deliberately is not.
#
# This repository stays private BECAUSE it now holds this (AGENTS.md,
# "Open items"). The exception below exists because the blanket workbook
# rule above would otherwise strip legitimate config files out of a tree
# that is meant to be a complete, checkable reference copy.
# ===================================================================
!production-reference/**/*.xlsx

# E23 working pack. Storage decision (git-lfs vs out-of-tree) is deliberately
# deferred, so the render is not blocked on it. MEASURED total is 3.34 GB, not the
# 819 MB of delivered audio alone: 811 MB PCM + 2,433 MB of 24 kHz masters that
# render() also writes + 97 MB TTS cache. Size storage for 3.3 GB.
asr-eval-v2/

# E24 working pack -- the same corpus with the product labels corrected, rendered into its
# own root rather than over v2. The plan's stamping policy is the reason: "No hash in this
# file may be recomputed after the freeze -- a changed hash is a new experiment id." E23's
# corpus has to stay exactly as E23 read it for its numbers to remain checkable, so a
# corrected corpus is a new root and a new experiment, never an edit in place.
# Ignored before it exists, so no window opens where 3 GB of audio is committable.
asr-eval-v3/
